      "role": "user",
      "content": "exactly. and that's what's so unsettling. it's not just that it looked \"off,\" it's that it looked like it was being *calculated*. if the micro-movements aren't there, then the \"humanity\" is just a skin. i've been following this theory that the real [Celebrity Name] hasn't actually been seen in public for years and what we're seeing in these recent press tours is just a highly sophisticated, perfecter-than-real proxy meant to maintain the brand while the actual person is... elsewhere. given how much more \"precise\" and \"smooth\" these recent appearances have been compared to how they used to be, does it make sense that we'd be looking at a digital or synthetic construction instead of the actual person?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
